&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring Ranges:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Remote Germany&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€57.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€76.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/mozilla/ios-software-engineer-189660","tags":["Firefox"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1793818523},{"slug":"robotics-operator-working-student-20hrs-week-berlin-435369","company_name":"Sensmore","title":"Robotics Operator - Working Student (20hrs / week)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">sensmore is a Berlin/Potsdam-based robotics startup delivering production-proven automation for industries where the world’s raw materials are extracted, moved, and processed. Its automation system transforms heavy machines into intelligent, automated robots powered by Physical AI and vertically integrates them into the full production environment: from the machine and safety infrastructure to network infrastructure, site processes, and operational interfaces. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Co-developed with customers, sensmore is backed by Point Nine Capital, leading industry investors, the State of Brandenburg, and the European Union.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Robot Operation &amp; Safety Supervision:</strong><br />Operate and supervise our autonomous machines during training and testing sessions, mainly remotely from the office and occasionally on site. Act as the safety supervisor, monitoring every run closely and stepping in when something doesn’t look right.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Readiness Checks &amp; Documentation:</strong><br />Complete pre-operation checklists to confirm each machine is safe and ready to run. Keep clear, accurate records of sessions, incidents and anomalies.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical Troubleshooting:</strong><br />Monitor systems during operation, carry out first-line checks and collect the data our engineers need. Escalate issues with concise, well-structured reports.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Testing Support:</strong><br />Help run test sessions, log results and feed your observations back to the engineering team to improve machine performance and test procedures.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Currently enrolled at a university</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A valid driving licence, held for at least 2 years, and confidence behind the wheel (mandatory)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A responsible, safety-conscious approach to every task</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Diligent, thorough and well organised, with a strong troubleshooting mindset</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical understanding: you’re a PC power user</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexibility on shift patterns, including evenings, fitting around your studies</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid technical understanding: comfortable working in the terminal / Linux, ideally with experience of observability tools (e.g. Grafana, Prometheus)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with heavy machinery or construction equipment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A deeper understanding of testing processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to work night shifts</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We Offer:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build physical AI for the world's largest off-highway machinery – making them intelligent, safe, and ready for every tough task</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join the pioneer in intelligent robotics backed by Point Nine &amp; other Tier 1 investors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Combine cutting-edge robotics research in end-to-end learning &amp; Vision Language Action Model with real-world heavy mobile equipment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tailor your own career path, whether you like to become technical specialist or technical team lead</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience a great team culture, beverages, and an amazing office environment</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>Benefits:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Attractive compensation package and stock options.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Beverages on-site and regular social events.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engage with top-tier researchers, engineers, and thought leaders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Influence the future of robotic technologies and tackle significant technological challenges.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assistance with relocation to Berlin.</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>About Us:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Heavy machinery, light years ahead.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">sensmore automates the world's largest machines with unprecedented intelligence. Our proprietary Physical AI enables heavy machines such as wheel loaders to instantly adapt to dynamic environments and execute new tasks without prior training.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We integrate cutting-edge robotics into a platform powering intelligence and automation products - transforming productivity and safety for customers in mining, construction, and adjacent industries today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are proudly backed by Point Nine and other Tier 1 investors.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/sensmore/robotics-operator-working-student-20hrs-week-berlin-435369","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin Office","created_at":1793817617},{"slug":"remote-senior-solutions-engineer-commercial-482484","company_name":"Clickup","title":"Senior Solutions Engineer, Commercial","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">At ClickUp, we're building the future of work: the first truly converged AI workspace unifying tasks, docs, chat, calendar, and enterprise search, all supercharged by context-driven AI. We are an AI-native company. Every team member is expected to leverage AI daily, and we evaluate AI fluency as part of our hiring process. Join us and help redefine what's possible. 🚀</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At ClickUp, we’re building an AI-powered workspace that brings tasks, docs, chat, and AI-enabled workflows together so teams can spend less time switching tools and more time making progress. Our mission is to make the world more productive. Within Solutions Engineering &amp; Customer Enablement, this role connects complex customer needs to practical product solutions, helping prospects and customers evaluate how ClickUp can support their workflows and business goals.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a customer-facing technical partner to Sales and Success, you’ll lead discovery, shape solution strategy, and turn technical questions into clear next steps. You’ll help customers see what’s possible with ClickUp while keeping recommendations grounded in real workflows, integration needs, and adoption considerations.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mission</strong></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help prospects and customers understand how ClickUp can solve meaningful workflow and productivity challenges through strong technical discovery, practical solution design, and credible guidance throughout the buying journey.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Accomplish</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Sales and Success to lead technical discovery, deliver tailored demos, and show how ClickUp, integrations, and AI-enabled workflows map to customer needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and lead proof-of-value or proof-of-concept work so buyers can validate product fit, adoption potential, and business impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate stakeholder requirements into clear solution recommendations, including workflow design, reporting approaches, and lightweight technical architecture.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support technical validation in live opportunities, including integration discussions, data migration considerations, security and process questions, and RFP responses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build custom reports, dashboards, and demo environments that reflect real customer use cases and make the platform concrete and credible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay current on product capabilities and releases so you can explain solutions accurately and connect new features to customer needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Account Executives, Customer Success, Product, and Engineering to remove blockers and improve the customer experience.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a customer-facing technical role in software, such as pre-sales, solutions engineering, sales engineering, technical consulting, implementation, or a closely related path.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated ability to lead technical discovery, live demos, and solution conversations with business and technical stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to turn ambiguous customer problems into structured recommendations, persuasive narratives, and practical next steps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort discussing APIs, integrations, automation, data flows, and change-management considerations in clear, customer-friendly language.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong presentation and executive communication skills, with the ability to influence technical and non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Consultative, outcomes-oriented judgment that balances technical depth with commercial urgency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to manage multiple customer opportunities and priorities with ownership, adaptability, and clear follow-through.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting complex B2B SaaS evaluations with multiple stakeholders and proof-of-value work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with workflow, collaboration, productivity, CRM, support, or automation platforms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with integration platforms, web services, APIs, or adjacent solution-design tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with business process mapping, value-based selling, and technical storytelling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to AI-enabled product workflows and the ability to explain their practical customer value.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location &amp; Travel</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">This U.S.-aligned role supports AMER customers and internal partners and requires effective collaboration across U.S. business hours.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is fully remote within the United States. </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equal Opportunity Employer </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>ClickUp is an Equal Opportunity Employer, and qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Privacy Notice</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>ClickUp collects and processes personal data in accordance with applicable data protection laws. You can find further details by viewing our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://clickup.com/careers-terms/candidate-privacy-notice"><em>Global Candidate Privacy Notice.</em></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>If you are a Philippine Job Applicant, please also see our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://t333.s.clickup-attachments-stg.com/t333/d9a53ce2-6d2c-48cd-84b1-ed4e525f9613/Philippine%20Data%20Privacy%20Notice_2024.pdf?view=open"><em>Philippine Data Privacy Notice</em></a><em> for further details.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Visa Sponsorship</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Please note we are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa for roles outside of engineering and product at this time. Sponsorship for engineering and product roles is not guaranteed, but is instead based on the business needs for that specific role at that time. Please reach out to the recruiter with any questions.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fraud Alert</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>ClickUp Talent Acquisition will only initiate contact via an <strong>@</strong></em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://clickup.com"><em><strong>clickup.com</strong></em></a><em> email or through our official careers portal on </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://clickup.com"><em>clickup.com</em></a><em>. We will never request fees, payments, or sensitive personal information. Please disregard any offers received outside these channels and report them to ----- style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI Processing Notice</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>ClickUp may use artificial intelligence and machine learning technologies to help review and screen candidates' employment applications against role-related criteria. These tools support, but do not replace, human decision‑making. If you have questions or need an accommodation in the recruitment process, please contact us at ----- $145K – $185K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • $145K – $185K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/clickup/remote-senior-solutions-engineer-commercial-482484","tags":["Customer Experience"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1793817616},{"slug":"senior-product-manager-integrations-ai-foundations-berlin-295355","company_name":"bunch","title":"Senior Product Manager | Integrations & AI Foundations (f/m/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.bunch.capital/"><u>bunch</u></a> is building the backbone of private markets. We are enabling next-gen fund operations with one integrated system that combines secure data infrastructure, AI-powered workflows and expert fund services. If you value ownership, growth through real responsibility, and working with a thoughtful, ambitious team, this role might be for you.</p><h1></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Your Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As <strong>Senior Product Manager</strong> for<strong> Integrations &amp; AI Foundations</strong>, you're the product owner for bunch's integration and AI platform. You have two kinds of customers: external developers and fund-manager teams connecting to bunch, and the internal product teams building on top of what this team provides.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Integrations &amp; AI Foundations is a new platform squad. It owns the infrastructure that lets data move securely between bunch and other systems, and lets every other product team build AI capabilities — extraction, retrieval, agents and evaluations — without each one solving the same hard problems again.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The team covers five connected areas:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Integrations / API layer</strong> — API contracts, authentication, versioning and deprecation, rate limits, uptime and SLA, and a Developer Portal</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>MCP layer</strong> — agent-callable tools built as thin wrappers over the same API contracts, including a customer-facing MCP offering</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Document Parsing</strong> — a reusable ingestion, decomposition and extraction pipeline, with human-in-the-loop review and accuracy monitoring</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Retrieval / RAG</strong> — chunking, embedding, vector store and retrieval, with access control enforced on every query, offered as a callable service</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI Agentic Layer</strong> — the agent framework, memory, guardrails, evaluation harness, observability and agent registry other teams use to ship their own agents</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Document extraction, agent workflows, evaluations and multi-provider model fallback under EU data residency are already in production. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fund managers don't want to retype data that already lives in their own systems, and they want to pull their bunch data into their own tools and their own AI. Customers and prospects ask for APIs, CRM and accounting syncs, automated exports of capital accounts, and MCP access. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll turn those signals into a coherent platform: one that customers integrate with, and that our own product teams build on, instead of a string of one-off builds.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You will:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Set platform strategy and sequencing</strong> across the five areas: decide how to slice the work and what ships first</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run APIs as a product</strong>: contracts, versioning and deprecation policy, rate limits, SLAs, Developer Portal and documentation, and time-to-integrate as a measure you actively drive down</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Define and launch the customer-facing MCP offering</strong>: which capabilities get exposed, tool descriptions that agents actually invoke correctly, and a security review gate for anything customers touch</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Generalise document parsing</strong>: the first use case is already live; your goal will be to take it over and generalise it so more teams can reuse its logic</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shape retrieval and the agentic layer as services</strong> other teams consume, with access control, guardrails, evaluations and observability built in rather than bolted on</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Draw and hold ownership lines</strong> with domain teams. When a request doesn't map to a named responsibility, run the scoping conversation rather than absorbing it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own platform-wide policy</strong> with Engineering and Security: data classification and residency, LLM cost and rate governance, and an integration and extraction registry so nothing gets built twice</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work directly with customers</strong> — fund managers, CFOs and their technical teams — and with Customer Success to understand integration needs, then turn them into platform decisions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Define success</strong> through goals and key results and clear metrics per area: API uptime and SLA, time-to-integrate, MCP adoption, extraction accuracy, and reuse across teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What success looks like</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In your first 90 days</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Resolve and document the MCP audience, governance model, and hand-off point between platform and domain teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Agree a plan and timeline for moving extraction from the existing team onto the shared pipeline</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define a sequenced first slice, with baseline metrics for each area</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In your first year</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A versioned public API and Developer Portal that customers integrate with</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A customer-facing MCP offering live</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Multiple domain teams extracting from their documents on the shared pipeline, shipping an agent on the agentic layer, without having to run a separate vector store or having to rebuild extraction from scratch</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>About you</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">6+ years in product management, with at least 3 on platform, API or developer-facing products in B2B SaaS</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've shipped and run public APIs: REST or GraphQL, OAuth and other authentication patterns, versioning, deprecation, and docs developers actually like</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience shipping LLM features to production, whether extraction, RAG or agents. You understand evaluations, confidence scoring, failure modes and human-in-the-loop review, and can hold your own with Applied AI engineers on chunking, embeddings and model fallback</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of MCP or agent tool-use, and a clear view on what makes a tool safe and reliable for an agent to call</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong instincts for security and compliance with regulated data: access control, GDPR and data residency</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You lead through influence. You're comfortable with internal teams as customers and can say no, or not us, clearly and with reasons</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You write clearly and document decisions so others can build on them</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fintech, fund administration or private markets experience: capital calls, capital accounts, subscription documents, LP and portfolio reporting</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in an EU-regulated environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've built a Developer Portal or a partner integrations programme from zero</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've moved a capability out of one team and into a shared platform without breaking either side</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a company moving from ops-led to product-led</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Workplace &amp; Benefits</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customizable benefits package (wellbeing, sport, mobility, food, and more)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">28 days of vacation, plus 2 company days and local public holidays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remote-flexible hybrid (3 days/week in office)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Up to 6 remote calendar weeks a year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A great tech and work setup</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with a diverse team of 120+ bunchies from 40+ countries, with leaders who are best-in-class in their domains</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Hiring process</strong></h2><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First interview with the People team</strong> (30 min) – Get acquainted with bunch and explore alignment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hiring Manager Interview</strong> with the VP of Product (60 min) – Discuss the role, your experience and your goals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Case Interview</strong> with Product &amp; Design (60 min) – Demonstrate how you think, work and communicate, based on a small case shared beforehand</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Final meetings with key stakeholders</strong> (3 x 30 min) – Learn more about the vision and discuss open questions</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Curious to learn more?</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Get a feel for who we are, how we work, and what we’re building:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.