tyle="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><h3><strong>1. Integrations</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the integrations for each deployment, including SSO and SCIM, Microsoft 365, SharePoint and OneDrive, Google Workspace, Salesforce, document management and chat tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Configure and connect Wordsmith to customers’ wider AI and data stack through MCP</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build, test and harden integrations so they hold up in production, not just in a demo</p></li></ul><h3><strong>2. Identity, Security &amp; Access</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set up identity and access, including SSO with Okta, Entra ID and Google, user provisioning, roles and permissions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work through customers’ security reviews, IT questionnaires and data-handling requirements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make sure permissions in Wordsmith respect the permissions in the systems it connects to</p></li></ul><h3><strong>3. Technical Solution Design</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take the technical handover from Sales and confirm the customer’s systems landscape, constraints and integration scope</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design how data, documents and requests flow between Wordsmith and the customer’s tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advise customer IT on the right architecture for their environment and where the trade-offs sit</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Legal Engineers to agree what each integration needs to support the workflows, agents and playbooks they’re configuring</p></li></ul><h3><strong>4. Technical Delivery &amp; Escalation</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the technical workstream of each deployment, from environment setup and integration build through testing to go-live</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Diagnose and fix integration issues, and act as the escalation point for technical problems during rollout</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Know when a problem needs Engineering, and bring them a clear, reproducible case</p></li></ul><h3><strong>5. Improve How We Integrate</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn what you learn into reusable integration patterns, setup guides and technical runbooks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Feed connector gaps, API limitations and recurring requests back to Product and Engineering</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience deploying and integrating enterprise SaaS in customer environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong working knowledge of identity and access, including SSO (SAML, OIDC), SCIM provisioning, Okta, Entra ID or Google Workspace</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience integrating with the Microsoft 365 and SharePoint, Google Workspace or Salesforce ecosystems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with APIs, webhooks, authentication flows and reading technical documentation. You can script or write code where it helps</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with MCP or other ways of connecting AI systems to tools and data, or a strong appetite to learn</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Credible with customer IT and security teams. You can answer their questions and stand behind your architecture</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Methodical troubleshooter who isolates problems, reproduces them and fixes them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear communicator who can explain a technical decision to a non-technical stakeholder</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Typical backgr